  "closure": "Full author mathematical body retained. Exact Theorem3.18 statement1292–1299 and primary1300–1302 conclusion are preserved with all required new Section3 stability proofs742–1290, the initial shape-derivative/Hessian derivations and detailed Appendix3393–3522. The short Weyl conclusion is not admitted separately from the new singular-RHS polygonal PDE core. Classical Savare-Schimperna, Grisvard/Dauge and Weyl foundations remain explicit references. Original illustrations are assets; every mathematical statement, full proof and caption remains editable. Numerical-certification and global-conjecture units are unselected context.",
  "current_difficulty_reason": "Ordinary domain continuity in H1 does not control the shape-Hessian coefficients, because the material-derivative equations have singular right-hand sides and eigenspace orthogonality constraints. The authors obtain stronger polygon-uniform regularity, estimate the varying right-hand sides and build projection corrections while controlling the material derivatives and coefficient blocks. Those new analytic estimates supply the Holder modulus before the routine finite-dimensional Weyl eigenvalue bound, rather than treating Weyl's theorem as the difficult obligation.",
  "editorial_changes": [
    "Independent article layout and explicit source, scope and difficulty boundary",
    "Bibliography restored from exact matching cached publisher HTML with native math annotations",
    "Necessary native macro definitions retained; only publisher typography commands mapped to ordinary article equivalents",
